module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Stack.Functoriality.PushforwardStack
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Stack.Functoriality.PushforwardMorSheafCovering
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Stack.EffectiveDescentRefinement

/-!
# The pushforward of a stack along a continuous functor of sites

Let `u : 𝒞 ⥤ 𝒟` be a continuous functor of sites and `p : 𝒮 ⥤ 𝒟` a stack over `𝒟`. This file
proves Stacks 04WC, that the pushforward `u^p𝒮 ⥤ 𝒞` of
`StacksDraft.CategoryTheory.Sites.Stack.Functoriality` is a stack over `𝒞`, and Stacks 04WD, its
version for stacks in groupoids.

The three conditions of Stacks 026F are discharged in three different places: condition (1) is
Stacks 04WB, `CategoryTheory.StrictPullback.isFibered_structureFunctor`; condition (2) is
`CategoryTheory.StrictPullback.isMorSheaf_structureFunctor_toGrothendieck`; condition (3) is
`CategoryTheory.StrictPullback.isEffective_of_preservesBaseChanges`, together with the locality
of effective descent `CategoryTheory.Functor.hasEffectiveDescent_of_refinements`.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.StrictPullback.isStack_structureFunctor_toGrothendieck`, Stacks 04WC;
* `CategoryTheory.StrictPullback.isStack_isFiberedInGroupoids_structureFunctor_toGrothendieck`,
  Stacks 04WD.

## Implementation notes

A site in the sense of Stacks 00VH is a category with a set of coverings, and is rendered here as
a precoverage `J₀ : Precoverage 𝒞` with the axioms of 00VH: `[J₀.HasIsos]`,
`[J₀.IsStableUnderComposition]`, `[J₀.IsStableUnderBaseChange]` and `[J₀.HasPullbacks]` (the
fibre products `Vⱼ ×_V T` of the members of a covering with an arbitrary morphism exist). Stacks
over the site are stacks for the Grothendieck topology `J₀.toGrothendieck` the coverings generate,
whose covering sieves are exactly the sieves containing a covering
(`CategoryTheory.Precoverage.mem_toGrothendieck_iff_of_isStableUnderComposition`). A continuous
functor of sites in the sense of Stacks 00WU is a functor `u` with

1. `J₀ ≤ K₀.comap u`: the image `{u(Vⱼ) ⟶ u(V)}` of a covering of `𝒞` is a covering of `𝒟`;
2. for every covering `{Vⱼ ⟶ V}` of `𝒞` and every morphism `T ⟶ V`, `u` preserves the fibre
   product `Vⱼ ×_V T`, i.e. `u(Vⱼ ×_V T) ⟶ u(Vⱼ) ×_{u(V)} u(T)` is an isomorphism.

Nothing else is assumed: `𝒞` need not have other fibre products, and `u` need not commute with
other fibre products. Of the site `(𝒟, K₀)` only its coverings are used, so its axioms are not
assumed either; the statement for a site `𝒟` in the sense of 00VH is the special case.

"Stack in groupoids" is read as the conjunction of `CategoryTheory.Functor.IsStack` (Stacks 026F)
and `CategoryTheory.Functor.IsFiberedInGroupoids` (Stacks 003S), as in
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Stack.Functoriality.PushforwardStack`.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace CategoryTheory

open Limits

universe v₁ v₂ v₃ u₁ u₂ u₃

variable {𝒞 : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} 𝒞] {𝒟 : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} 𝒟]
  {𝒮 : Type u₃} [Category.{v₃} 𝒮]

namespace StrictPullback

/-- The pushforward `u^p𝒮 ⥤ 𝒞` of a stack `p : 𝒮 ⥤ 𝒟` over `(𝒟, K)` is a stack over the site
`(𝒞, J₀)` given by coverings, for a functor `u` sending the coverings of `J₀` to families
generating covering sieves of `K`, and commuting with the fibre products of the members of the
coverings of `J₀` with arbitrary morphisms. This is the form of Stacks 04WC in which the target
site is given by a Grothendieck topology; see the implementation notes.

Condition (2) of Stacks 026F is
`CategoryTheory.StrictPullback.isMorSheaf_structureFunctor_toGrothendieck`. For condition (3),
effective descent is local on the base once condition (2) holds
(`CategoryTheory.Functor.hasEffectiveDescent_of_refinements`), so it suffices to treat the sieve
generated by a covering `P` of `J₀`, which every covering sieve contains; that is
`CategoryTheory.StrictPullback.isEffective_of_preservesBaseChanges`. -/
theorem isStack_structureFunctor_of_generate_map_mem (J₀ : Precoverage 𝒞) [J₀.HasIsos]
    [J₀.IsStableUnderComposition] [J₀.IsStableUnderBaseChange] [J₀.HasPullbacks]
    (K : GrothendieckTopology 𝒟) (u : 𝒞 ⥤ 𝒟)
    (hcov : ∀ ⦃V : 𝒞⦄ ⦃R : Presieve V⦄, R ∈ J₀ V → Sieve.generate (R.map u) ∈ K (u.obj V))
    (hpres : ∀ ⦃V : 𝒞⦄ ⦃R : Presieve V⦄, R ∈ J₀ V → ∀ ⦃W : 𝒞⦄ ⦃f : W ⟶ V⦄, R f →
      ∀ ⦃T : 𝒞⦄ (g : T ⟶ V), PreservesLimit (cospan f g) u)
    (p : 𝒮 ⥤ 𝒟) (hp : Functor.IsStack p K) :
    Functor.IsStack (structureFunctor u p) J₀.toGrothendieck := by
  have := hp.isFibered
  have hmor := isMorSheaf_structureFunctor_toGrothendieck J₀ K u hcov hpres p hp.isMorSheaf
  refine { isFibered := inferInstance, isMorSheaf := hmor, hasEffectiveDescent := ?_ }
  refine Functor.hasEffectiveDescent_of_refinements hmor fun U R hR => ?_
  obtain ⟨P, hP, hle⟩ := J₀.mem_toGrothendieck_iff_of_isStableUnderComposition.1 hR
  refine ⟨Sieve.generate P, (Sieve.generate_le_iff _ _).2 hle,
    J₀.generate_mem_toGrothendieck hP, fun D => ?_⟩
  refine isEffective_of_preservesBaseChanges K hp.hasEffectiveDescent D
    (fun V f hf => Sieve.le_generate P V f hf) (fun V f hf T g => ?_) (fun V f hf => ?_) (hcov hP)
  · have : P.HasPullbacks g := J₀.hasPullbacks_of_mem g hP
    have : HasPullback f g := Presieve.hasPullback g hf
    have : PreservesLimit (cospan f g) u := hpres hP hf g
    exact ⟨hasPullback_symmetry f g, preservesPullback_symmetry u f g⟩
  · obtain ⟨W, k, f₀, hf₀, rfl⟩ := hf
    exact ⟨_, u.map k, u.map f₀, Presieve.map_map hf₀, (u.map_comp _ _).symm⟩

/-- **Stacks 04WC**.
Let `(𝒞, J₀)` be a site in the sense of Stacks 00VH, given by its coverings `J₀`, and let
`(𝒟, K₀)` be a category with coverings `K₀`. Let `u : 𝒞 ⥤ 𝒟` be a continuous functor of sites in
the sense of Stacks 00WU: `u` sends coverings to coverings (`J₀ ≤ K₀.comap u`), and for every
covering `{Vⱼ ⟶ V}` of `𝒞` and every morphism `T ⟶ V` it commutes with the fibre product
`Vⱼ ×_V T` (`hpres`). If `p : 𝒮 ⥤ 𝒟` is a stack over `𝒟`, then the pushforward `u^p𝒮 ⥤ 𝒞` is
a stack over `𝒞`.

Stacks over the sites are stacks for the Grothendieck topologies their coverings generate; see
the implementation notes. -/
@[stacks 04WC]
theorem isStack_structureFunctor_toGrothendieck (J₀ : Precoverage 𝒞) [J₀.HasIsos]
    [J₀.IsStableUnderComposition] [J₀.IsStableUnderBaseChange] [J₀.HasPullbacks]
    (K₀ : Precoverage 𝒟) (u : 𝒞 ⥤ 𝒟) (hu : J₀ ≤ K₀.comap u)
    (hpres : ∀ ⦃V : 𝒞⦄ ⦃R : Presieve V⦄, R ∈ J₀ V → ∀ ⦃W : 𝒞⦄ ⦃f : W ⟶ V⦄, R f →
      ∀ ⦃T : 𝒞⦄ (g : T ⟶ V), PreservesLimit (cospan f g) u)
    (p : 𝒮 ⥤ 𝒟) (hp : Functor.IsStack p K₀.toGrothendieck) :
    Functor.IsStack (structureFunctor u p) J₀.toGrothendieck :=
  isStack_structureFunctor_of_generate_map_mem J₀ K₀.toGrothendieck u
    (fun _ _ hR => K₀.generate_mem_toGrothendieck (hu _ hR)) hpres p hp

/-- **Stacks 04WD**.
Let `(𝒞, J₀)` be a site in the sense of Stacks 00VH, `(𝒟, K₀)` a category with coverings, and
`u : 𝒞 ⥤ 𝒟` a continuous functor of sites in the sense of Stacks 00WU, as in
`CategoryTheory.StrictPullback.isStack_structureFunctor_toGrothendieck`. If `p : 𝒮 ⥤ 𝒟` is a
stack in groupoids over `𝒟`, then the pushforward `u^p𝒮 ⥤ 𝒞` is a stack in groupoids over `𝒞`.

As in the source, the proof is Stacks 04WC together with the fact that the fibre categories of
`u^p𝒮` are groupoids (`CategoryTheory.StrictPullback.isFiberedInGroupoids_structureFunctor`).
Neither all fibre products in `𝒞` nor their preservation by `u` is assumed; the version that
assumes both is `CategoryTheory.StrictPullback.isStack_isFiberedInGroupoids_structureFunctor`. -/
@[stacks 04WD "a stack in groupoids (Stacks 02ZI) is rendered as `Functor.IsStack` together with \
  `Functor.IsFiberedInGroupoids`; stacks over a site given by coverings are stacks for the \
  Grothendieck topology the coverings generate"]
theorem isStack_isFiberedInGroupoids_structureFunctor_toGrothendieck (J₀ : Precoverage 𝒞)
    [J₀.HasIsos] [J₀.IsStableUnderComposition] [J₀.IsStableUnderBaseChange] [J₀.HasPullbacks]
    (K₀ : Precoverage 𝒟) (u : 𝒞 ⥤ 𝒟) (hu : J₀ ≤ K₀.comap u)
    (hpres : ∀ ⦃V : 𝒞⦄ ⦃R : Presieve V⦄, R ∈ J₀ V → ∀ ⦃W : 𝒞⦄ ⦃f : W ⟶ V⦄, R f →
      ∀ ⦃T : 𝒞⦄ (g : T ⟶ V), PreservesLimit (cospan f g) u)
    (p : 𝒮 ⥤ 𝒟) (hp : Functor.IsStack p K₀.toGrothendieck) (hp' : p.IsFiberedInGroupoids) :
    Functor.IsStack (structureFunctor u p) J₀.toGrothendieck ∧
      (structureFunctor u p).IsFiberedInGroupoids :=
  ⟨isStack_structureFunctor_toGrothendieck J₀ K₀ u hu hpres p hp,
    isFiberedInGroupoids_structureFunctor u p hp'⟩

end StrictPullback

end CategoryTheory
